Description: depth layers: a layer group at one depth, each eye's picture, the pop and sink keys
 A depth layer (GimpDepthLayer, a layer group) holds its layers at one depth
 the artist sets, in pixels of separation with three decimals: positive
 behind the screen, negative in front of it, never clamped.  Layers in no
 depth layer are at the screen, so a 2D document is unchanged; a depth layer
 inside another is at its own value, never the sum.  The value is the
 group's persistent parasite "gimp-depth-layer" (the stereo policy library's
 text), so an XCF file keeps it and a GIMP without depth layers opens a plain
 layer group and loses nothing; xcf-load turns such a group into a depth
 layer again.
 .
 Each eye's picture (GimpEyeProjectable) composites the image's layers with
 copies of their mode nodes over the eye's own picture of what lies below,
 the layers' content and masks taken from the image's graph as they are and
 moved by the eye's half of the depth (gimp:depth-shift: a copy of the
 samples for a whole move, the stereo policy library's Lanczos resampling of
 premultiplied samples for a fractional one).  The stereo canvas shows it as
 a third kind of image; with the eye layers too, each eye shows its own eye
 layer under the depth layers; a packed picture in an editing mode keeps its
 depth layers at the screen and the status bar says so.
 .
 Layer > New Depth Layer puts the selected layers into a new depth layer.
 The Layers dock shows and edits the depth of the selected layer's depth
 layer (the row is hidden otherwise).  The actions layers-depth-pop (8) and
 layers-depth-sink (7), held over the canvas, turn the pointer's movement into
 depth, 0.1 pixel of separation for each pixel moved, one undo step for each
 gesture; from the menu each moves the depth by one pixel.  The PDB gains
 gimp-depth-layer-new, -get-depth, -set-depth and -new-from-eye, for the
 core only (pdb/groups/depth_layer.pdb exports nothing to libgimp).
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Origin: other, Sparky Stereo OS (queue row 137 with row 148, the stereo GIMP's milestone 2)
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-26
